# Python conventions

- Python 3.12. Full type hints; code must pass `mypy --strict`. No `Any` unless justified in a comment.
- Data crossing module boundaries = Pydantic models or frozen dataclasses. No loose dicts.
- Modules: `ingest` (load/parse/chunk), `retrieval` (index/search/rerank), `llm` (LLM clients, prompts, structured output), `classify` (clause model train/infer), `evals` (metrics, harness, CLI), `api` (FastAPI routes only — thin; business logic lives in the other modules).
- `api` may import other modules; other modules must NOT import `api`.
- External clients (DB, Gemini, HF) are created in one place and injected (FastAPI `Depends` or constructor args) so tests can swap fakes.
- Use `logging.getLogger(__name__)`; no `print` in src.
- Raise specific exceptions; never bare `except:`. Don't swallow errors silently.
- Pure functions where possible; side effects (network, disk) at the edges.
- Docstrings on public functions: one-line summary + Args/Returns when non-obvious.
